  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-41302-PMR26-BRA107</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-41302" type="40">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Labour Organization (ILO)</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved public policies to promote care economy, gender equality and equality of treatment and opportunities for all</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Country Programme Outcome (CPO) supports Brazil in advancing gender equality, non-discrimination, and inclusion in the world of work, in a context marked by persistent structural inequalities affecting women&#x2014;particularly Black women&#x2014;and other vulnerable groups. It promotes the integration of gender-responsive and intersectional approaches into public policies, with a strong focus on the care economy, equal pay, and the elimination of discrimination and violence in the workplace, while reinforcing the role of social dialogue and international labour standards.
The expected outputs include the generation of evidence through studies on equal remuneration, access to care policies, vulnerable groups, and inclusive labour market participation, as well as capacity-building initiatives to strengthen the implementation of the National Care Policy and promote decent work in care and domestic work. Additional efforts to disseminate international labour standards, including those related to violence and harassment, will support improved prevention and response mechanisms. These actions are expected to enhance institutional and tripartite capacities to design and implement inclusive policies, contributing to reduced gender and racial inequalities, improved working conditions, expanded access to decent work, and more equitable and resilient labour market outcomes in Brazil.</narrative>
  </description>
